   "text": {
    "L1": "A magnet does not attract every metal. We must test each material.",
    "L2": "Magnets attract iron, nickel, cobalt, and steels that contain iron.",
    "L3": "Aluminium, copper and brass are metals, but they are not attracted. Plastic, wood, paper, rubber and glass are not attracted either.",
    "L4": "So a shiny or metal-looking object is not automatically magnetic.",
    "L5": "In our example, test the iron tawa, foil, steel spoon and plastic lid one at a time.",
    "L6": "Record each result, then group the objects as attracted or not attracted.",
    "L7": "A magnet can act through paper, cloth, glass and water. It can even pull a paper clip through a glass of water.",
    "L8": "Two steel spoons can behave differently, so testing is the reliable way to sort materials."
   },
